.TH STDOUT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
stdout \- Crunch standard output stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.B struct FILE* stdout;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B stdout
is the initially open, unbuffered Crunch stream for file descriptor 1.
It can be passed to Crunch stream functions and closed with
.BR fclose (3crunch).
After closing it the stream pointer is invalid.
.SH NOTES
Crunch stream objects are not C library
.B FILE
objects. The standard stream names are macros referring to Crunch-specific
global pointers; they do not interoperate with libc's stream objects.
Direct descriptor output and Crunch's
.B print
and
.B printf
do not update this stream's indicators.
Crunch streams and errno are not thread-safe.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stdin (3crunch),
.BR stderr (3crunch),
.BR fputc (3crunch),
.BR fclose (3crunch)
